            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary thrombosis and ectasia of coronary arteries after long-term use of anabolic steroids].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>326-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic abuse of anabolic steroids is widespread. Hypertrophy of skeletal and heart muscle is a well-known effect of chronic anabolic steroid abuse. Structural alterations of blood vessels are new side effects. We report a case of a 32-year-old bodybuilder after long-term use of anabolic steroids who died of cardiac arrest. Coronary angiography and autopsy findings showed especially a hypertrophic heart, structural changes of coronary arteries, intracoronary thrombosis and myocardial infarction, ventricular thrombosis and systemic embolism</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
